  Interpretation: REGIME_STABLE = the candidate behaves the same way (same edge or no edge) across regimes; REGIME_STABLE_LOSS = the candidate loses money in every regime mix (stable losses, not an edge, and the verdict must be read alongside the medians); REGIME_DEPENDENT = results swing strongly across regimes relative to the coin-flip null (fits one regime); CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE = indistinguishable from noise in every segment.

